## 3. What nova_validation actually is

$ grep -n "nova_validation" src/orb/live/upstream/nova-sonic-live-client.ts
-> :80  if (name === 'ValidationException' || status === 400) return 'nova_validation';
   i.e. ANY ValidationException or HTTP 400 maps to this label.

$ full diagnostic (untruncated) for the blocked session
-> "RequestId=... : Error(s):\nError 1 : This request has been blocked by our
   content filters."  — in THIS case genuinely a guardrail, no field detail.

Also ruled out oversize: DEFAULT_INSTRUCTION_CHUNK_BYTES = 4_000
(nova-sonic-config.ts:152) chunks the system instruction, and the greeting is
only 319 chars.

## 4. The guided-only difference in the greeting payload

$ read src/services/conversation/compute-greeting-decision.ts
-> wakeTrigger  (non-guided): "...Compose the wording yourself ... do not
                               recite the lead word for word"      -> passes
-> guidedTrigger (guided):    "Open by saying this prepared line: "<safe>"
                               ... do not turn it into something else"
                                                                   -> 0/93
A verbatim-reproduction directive fenced by prohibitions. Matches the
Vertex-worked / Nova-broke report: Bedrock guardrail, no Vertex equivalent.
VTID-03674 removed the HARSHER wrapper but replaced it with a milder VERBATIM
one, which is why that fix did not move the number.

## 5. SECOND DEFECT — two copies, and the live path was the other one

$ grep -n "guidedTrigger" src/services/conversation/compute-greeting-decision.ts
-> ~705 tryGuidedTopicRung   (copy A)
-> ~1082 rung 8              (copy B)
Byte-identical copies under a comment claiming the ladders "can never drift
apart on this again".

PRODUCTION USES COPY A: every blocked session's greeting_sent carries
`guided_topic_outranks_passive_rungs: true`, set only by tryGuidedTopicRung.
Proven live: after editing copy B only, `jest -t "guided-teach"` still PASSED
against the OLD string — the edit was invisible to the live path.

## 6. Fix

Extracted ONE `buildGuidedTopicOpenTrigger()`; both ladders call it. Template
describes the opening and interpolates NOTHING (no topic title, no practice
target, no per-language text) — the GUIDE MODE block already names them. That
is what makes it correct for all 254 topics and every locale with no table to
keep in sync.

$ npx tsc --noEmit                      -> clean
$ grep -rn "do not turn it into something else" src/  -> only inside a comment

## 7. Tests re-recorded deliberately (4 assertions, 2 files)

Each pinned the OLD verbatim behaviour as correct; each now asserts the NEW
invariant instead (line must NOT be embedded), with reasoning inline:
  - golden: rung 8 guided-teach   (/ONE short utterance/ -> compositional +
                                   explicit not.toMatch of both old phrases)
  - golden: normal ladder collision  (toContain -> not.toContain)
  - golden: safe-fast ladder collision (toContain -> not.toContain)
            + NEW anti-drift assertion: both ladders emit the IDENTICAL
              directive (toBe), so copy-drift cannot recur
  - conversation-flow-regression: guided does not get three-beat contract
Every pre-existing invariant in those tests (guided WINS the collision, no
NEXT STEP/CONFIRMATION, no fluent/translate, briefing not stamped) is
unchanged and still passing.

$ npx jest test/services/conversation/compute-greeting-decision.golden.test.ts
PASS -- 59/59, 1 snapshot re-recorded (only the guided directive changed;
        confirmed the old wording is gone from the .snap and the new is in)

